# Contributing

Thanks for helping. Bug reports, results from other models, ideas, and pull requests are
all welcome. This project follows a [Code of Conduct](CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md) and the
maintainer's [integration standard](https://github.com/jasonaward/ha-integration-standards).

## Reporting

### Bugs

Use the [bug report form](https://github.com/jasonaward/{{ repo }}/issues/new/choose).
Attach a diagnostics download: on the device page, select the three dots menu >
**Download diagnostics**. Downloads are designed to leave out private fields, but look
them over before posting.

If asked for a debug log:

1. On the integration's page, select the three dots menu > **Enable debug logging**.
2. Make the problem happen again, and note the time.
3. Select **Disable debug logging**; Home Assistant offers the log as a download.
4. Look it over before posting, and remove anything you'd rather not share.

### A new or untested model

Use the bug report form, tick **This is a new or untested model**, and include:

- the {{ device }}'s model and firmware (on the device page);
- a diagnostics download;
- which entities show sensible values, and which don't;
- which actions worked;
- anything wrong or missing compared with the {{ company or "manufacturer" }}'s app.

### Security

Report vulnerabilities privately, as described in [SECURITY.md](SECURITY.md), never in a
public issue.

## Development

```bash
python3 -m venv .venv && . .venv/bin/activate
pip install pytest-homeassistant -r requirements_test.txt -r requirements_ci.txt
pytest -q --cov=custom_components --cov-report=json
python scripts/check_coverage.py coverage.json 95
ruff check . && ruff format --check .
mypy
```

The rules that matter most:

- Never log passwords, tokens, or full device IDs.
- No new dependencies without discussion first.
- Be gentle with the {{ device }}{% if company %} and {{ company }}'s service{% endif %}: no new polling without a limit.
- User-facing text goes in `translations/en.json`, never in code.
- Keep every module above 95% test coverage, and add a line to `CHANGELOG.md`.
- Use made-up values in tests and examples, never real emails, device IDs, serial
  numbers, or MAC addresses.

## AI-assisted contributions

They're welcome. Say so in the pull request. You're responsible for what you submit and
should understand it; it gets the same review and tests as any other change.

